# Copy to .env (gitignored, chmod 600) and fill in real values.
#
# EDUROAM_*           read by modules/core/network.nix; substituted into the
#                     NetworkManager eduroam profile at activation time, so a
#                     missing or empty value shows up as a failed wifi auth.
# VPN_IST_*           read by modules/core/network.nix; substituted into the
#                     NetworkManager "tecnico" OpenVPN profile. The identity is
#                     the Tecnico ID in full, istxxxxx@tecnico.ulisboa.pt.
# GITLAB_USER         GitLab account username; the credential helper sends it as
#                     the HTTPS username next to GITLAB_HTTPS. Optional —
#                     gitlab.com ignores the username for token auth, so an empty
#                     value falls back to "oauth2".
#
# Parsed by systemd (EnvironmentFile=), so: KEY=value, no `export`, no quotes
# unless the value genuinely contains them.
EDUROAM_IDENTITY=your-institutional-login@example.edu
EDUROAM_PASSWORD=your-eduroam-password-here
VPN_IST_IDENTITY=istxxxxxx@tecnico.ulisboa.pt
VPN_IST_PASSWORD=your-tecnico-password-here
GITLAB_USER=your-username
